Z||000000||pontiacs4me||03-09-2001||01:46 AM||||OK heres the deal now.  A little while ago I was driving home from a friends house and on the way I saw some friends at a gas station.  So I stopped to say hey, and when I was leaving one of these drunk friends was trying to jump on my trunk, so I nailed it and drove into another parking lot, on the way in there is a high section of the lot and the rear of the car got a little light and I went a little sideways.  I recovered and drove off normally without spinning out.  then after that the car wouldnt shift into 3rd gear (btw its an auto). I know it isnt low on fluid, I checked it this afternoon.  And it cant be going out, every tranny I ever had go out on me lost reverse first.  Reverse works fine.  I havent changed the fluid or filter since Ive owned it (900 miles now).  So Im doing that tomorrow.  Any ideas to what happened?  Any reasonable ($$$) ways to fix it?  I just need it and the engine to last until I have the money for the 3800 series II supercharged for it.  Which will probably be next winters project.  thanks for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||03-09-2001||02:41 PM||||Cheapest thing to try (I think) is see if the throttle valve (TV) cable needs adjusting.  Ogre's cave has a good description of the procedure, if I recall.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   ||||reg||5
Z||000002||theogre||03-09-2001||09:03 PM||||Checking TV cable wouldn't hurt. sounds more like something sin't happy about the bounce. may have shook some carp loose and blocked a passage in the valve body. Might could be the governor. If that is hung or crapped up you'll have shift problems.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||03-09-2001||10:39 PM||||Ok, this morning the tranny worked fine.  I got to my shop and I changed the filter and fluid.  I found a donut looking magnet in the bottom of the pan, Did they put those in there stock?  I think the tranny has been rebuilt, It looked real clean all inside and the input shaft seal was new looking when I did the swap.  Anyway there wasnt a whole lot of metal on the magnet, but some.  I put it all back together and its running even better now.  It shifts a little cleaner, and I run a lower rpm at crusin speeds.  I figured the tranny fluid has lost some viscosity, and the torque converter wasnt spooling out all the way.  Could this be the problem?  Anyway, i fixed the water leak, the tranny is running good.  I just finished 65 miles of pizza delivery tonight and everything is great.  <BR>Until tommorow......||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||03-10-2001||12:02 AM||||The magnet is stock. Well I have not changed the filter in my Fiero but in my Celebrity with 125C it had one just to catch all the meatllic crap that might be floating around.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||03-10-2001||11:44 AM||||The magnet belongs there. allot of GM's trannies have them. ||||reg||1
